<par def='1'><run><font size='9pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>3 - Created an Agent that removes or adds the tax (GST) on each projects, if the administrator mistakenly set the GST Exemption to 'Yes or No' from the start when creating the project financial code. This adjustment can be done from the </run><run
><font size='9pt' style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>View By Project</run><run><font size='9pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20'/> as shown in the image below. The two agent action bar buttons will only be visible to the administrator and will be labelled </run><run
><font size='9pt' style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>Add GST</run><run><font size='9pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20'/> and </run><run><font size='9pt' style='bold'
 name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Remove GST</run><run
><font size='9pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/> and will only act on selected documents. The Administrator must then </run><run
><font size='9pt' style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>Re-Calculate Budget</run><run><font size='9pt' name='Arial'
 pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/> within the project document.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font size='9pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/></run></par>
